{
  "id": "Lyo.FileTags.FFmpeg",
  "name": "Lyo.FileTags.FFmpeg",
  "area": "Data",
  "tagline": "ffprobe read and stream-copy write for audio and video tags.",
  "description": "Audio and video tags for [`Lyo.FileTags`](../Lyo.FileTags/README.md). Extensions are mp3, m4a, flac, wav, ogg, mp4, mov, mkv, and webm. Images are not claimed. Read merges ffprobe format tags over stream tags. Write is `-c copy`, optional `-map_metadata -1`, then `-metadata`. It does not re-encode. Convert-time `-metadata` during an encode stays in [`Lyo.FFmpeg`](../../Media/Lyo.FFmpeg/README.md).",
  "features": [
    "**Read.** Format `title` beats a stream `title`. An unknown name such as `composer` stays `FileTagKey.Custom`.",
    "**Write.** Stream copy onto a temp file, then replace. `ClearExisting` emits `-map_metadata -1` before `-c copy` and `-metadata`.",
    "**Paths.** `FFmpegOptions.FFmpegPath` and `FfprobePath`. Null uses the tools on PATH."
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Set a title without re-encoding",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "var tags = new FFmpegFileTagProvider(new FFmpegOptions());\nawait tags.WriteAsync(\"tone.wav\", new FileTagWriteRequest(new Dictionary<FileTagKey, string> {\n    [FileTagKey.Title] = \"Show\"\n}));"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Public types",
      "headers": [
        "Type",
        "Description"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "FFmpegFileTagProvider",
          "IFileTagReader and IFileTagWriter for audio and video extensions."
        ],
        [
          "Extensions",
          "AddFFmpegFileTags() and AddFFmpegFileTags(FFmpegOptions)."
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
